Host-only ARM64 BPF probe logic checks
======================================

Run with TEST_OUTPUT pointing outside the kernel source tree:
  TEST_OUTPUT=/absolute/output python3 tools/testing/selftests/bpf_arm64_probe/run-host.py

Requires a 64-bit native host, GCC, AddressSanitizer and UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer.
No root or tablet access is used. The runner extracts the actual exception-entry
builder/fixup/validation functions, the architecture exception dispatch and the
actual verifier guard generation statements. Source SHA256s and results are
saved in TEST_OUTPUT; generated files never enter the source tree.

Tests exercise all 31 possible destination-register slots and four load widths,
PC advance/zero destination with flags/SP unchanged, invalid table/count/range
handling and ordinary non-BPF exception behavior. A small instruction interpreter
checks the real generated guard over user/kernel/effective-offset/wrap/alias cases.

These are host fixtures with kernel-interface stubs, not generated ARM64 machine
code execution or induced kernel data aborts. Full kernel compilation, actual
Android BPF loading, accounting/lifetime stress and recovery tests remain required.
